3. No LLM access, processing, modification, or training

Subject to section 5, including rights separately granted under applicable
GitHub Terms of Service or another hosting agreement, this license grants
no permission to do any of the following, directly or through another
person, account, service, dataset, or intermediary:

(a) Give an LLM System access to Covered Material, or cause it to fetch, read,
    view, ingest, inspect, analyze, summarize, translate, answer questions
    about, review, generate changes to, modify, or otherwise process Covered
    Material. This includes AI coding assistants and agents, even when a
    human approves their output.

(b) Submit Covered Material as a prompt, context, attachment, tool response,
    screenshot, image input, retrieval source, or other input to an LLM
    System, or create embeddings, vector stores, or retrieval-augmented
    generation indexes for use by such a system from Covered Material.

(c) Use Covered Material to develop, pretrain, train, fine-tune, align,
    distill, evaluate, benchmark, or improve an LLM System, or create or
    augment a dataset for those purposes, including through synthetic
    examples or model-generated transformations of Covered Material.

(d) Sell, license, supply, or redistribute Covered Material specifically to
    facilitate a use prohibited by this section, or remove these conditions
    to enable such a use. Ordinary public redistribution for permitted human
    use is allowed subject to section 4.

Reading this license and an accompanying AI_POLICY.md solely to identify
and comply with their restrictions does not authorize processing any other
Covered Material. A separate, express permission from the relevant copyright
holders is required for a restricted use; possession of a public copy, a
paid account, a fork, or permission from an unrelated fork maintainer is not
such permission. Authorization for one specified maintenance task does not
authorize unrelated access, dataset collection, or model training.

